{"id":"neet-2025-q085","pn":85,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Thermodynamics (Chemistry)","st":"Enthalpy of formation, Hess's law","q":"The standard heat of formation, in kcal/mol of Ba²⁺ is :\n[Given : standard heat of formation of SO₄²⁻ ion (aq) = –216 kcal/mol, standard heat of crystallisation of BaSO₄(s) = –4.5 kcal/mol, standard heat of formation of BaSO₄(s) = – 349 kcal/mol]","o":["– 128.5","– 133.0","+ 133.0","+ 220.5"],"c":0,"s":"(1) S + 2O₂ + 2e⁻ → SO₄²⁻, ΔH_f = –216 kcal/mol\n(2) Ba²⁺(g) + SO₄²⁻(g) → BaSO₄(s), ΔH_crystallisation = –4.5 kcal/mol\n(3) Ba + S + 2O₂ → BaSO₄(s), ΔH_f(BaSO₄) = –349 kcal/mol\n(4) Ba(s) → Ba²⁺(g) + 2e⁻\nEquation (4) is obtained from (1), (2) and (3) by applying (3) – (1) – (2).\nSo, –349 – (–4.5) – (–216)\n= –349 + 4.5 + 216\n= –349 + 220.5\n= –128.5 kcal/mol"},
{"id":"neet-2024-q058","pn":58,"y":"NEET 2024 · 5 May","tp":"Thermodynamics (Chemistry)","st":"Types of thermodynamic processes","q":"Match the List I with List II.\nList-I (Process) — List-II (Conditions)\nA. Isothermal process — I. No heat exchange\nB. Isochoric process — II. Carried out at constant temperature\nC. Isobaric process — III. Carried out at constant volume\nD. Adiabatic process — IV. Carried out at constant pressure\nChoose the correct answer from the option given below :","o":["A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV","A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I","A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I","A-IV, B-II, C-III, D-I"],"c":1,"s":"(A) Isothermal: temperature stays constant.\n(B) Isochoric: volume stays constant.\n(C) Isobaric: pressure stays constant.\n(D) Adiabatic: no heat (q) is exchanged with the surroundings.\nMatch: A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-I."},
{"id":"neet-2024-q078","pn":78,"y":"NEET 2024 · 5 May","tp":"Thermodynamics (Chemistry)","st":"Entropy change","q":"In which of the following processes entropy increases ?\nA. A liquid evaporates to vapour.\nB. Temperature of a crystalline solid lowered from 130 K to 0 K.\nC. 2NaHCO₃(s) → Na₂CO₃(s) + CO₂(g) + H₂O(g)\nD. Cl₂(g) → 2Cl(g)\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :","o":["A, C and D","C and D","A and C","A, B and D"],"c":0,"s":"A: a liquid turning to vapour gives more disorder, so entropy increases.\nC: the number of gaseous product molecules increases, so entropy increases.\nD: 1 mol Cl₂(g) gives 2 mol Cl(g), so entropy increases.\nB: cooling a solid lowers its disorder, so entropy decreases.\nSo A, C and D."},
{"id":"neet-2024-q097","pn":97,"y":"NEET 2024 · 5 May","tp":"Thermodynamics (Chemistry)","st":"Work in reversible isothermal expansion","q":"The work done during reversible isothermal expansion of one mole of hydrogen gas at 25ºC from pressure of 20 atmosphere to 10 atmosphere is :\n(Given R = 2.0 cal K⁻¹ mol⁻¹)","o":["413.14 calories","100 calories","0 calories","–413.14 calories"],"c":3,"s":"For a reversible isothermal process, W = –2.303 nRT log(Pᵢ/P_f).\nW = –2.303 × 1 × 2 × 298 × log 2.\nW = –2.303 × 1 × 2 × 298 × 0.3.\nW = –413.14 calories."}
